################################################################################
# This .gitignore file was automatically created by Microsoft(R) Visual Studio.
################################################################################

/.vs
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Database files — never overwrite local data on pull
data/blipshell.db
data/blipshell.db-shm
data/blipshell.db-wal
# benchmark.db is now ONLY the refetchable discovery catalog; data/benchmark/
# The human-readable memory mirror is regenerated nightly from the DB and
# contains the distilled personal layer -- it must never reach the remote.
data/mirror/
# holds the generated report. Both are derivable, so both stay ignored.
data/benchmark.db
data/benchmark.db-shm
data/benchmark.db-wal
data/benchmark/

# DO NOT ignore benchmark_results/ — those files ARE the benchmark history and
# must be committed. They used to live in the gitignored benchmark.db, which is
# precisely why results never synced between the dev box and the Ollama PC and
# every report was missing models the other machine had measured.
!benchmark_results/
data/chroma/
data/.blipshell_history

# --- 2026-09-04 hardening: a near-miss almost pushed 2.5GB of personal data ---
# Ignore the data tree by default (the DB, backups, exports, images, snapshots
# and receipts all live under it; anything a script drops next to the DB is
# personal by default), carving out only the non-personal benchmark artifacts
# that must sync between machines. `data/*` not `data/` so the negations work.
data/*
!data/benchmark_coding_transcripts/
!data/.gitkeep
!data/search_ground_truth.json
!data/test_sample_ids.json
# DB copies and ad-hoc backup folders anywhere in the repo.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.backup.*
backups/
Clean DB/
blipshell/data/
blipshell/data - Copy/
# Command history, personal digest, telemetry.
.blipshell_history
.blipshell/
.deepeval/
# Agent-eval scratch files dropped in the repo root by benchmark stress runs.
stress_test_*
canned_test_scratch.py
graph.json
graph.html
reasoning_spike.txt
